# Vulnerabilities `make scan-lock` / `make scan-image` / `make publish-image` accept on purpose.
#
# Same format and rules as steps/train/distill/images/gpu/scan-ignore: one advisory id per
# line (CVE, GHSA or PYSEC; list every alias, because trivy and osv-scanner name the same
# advisory differently, and take them from the advisory record's aliases on osv.dev rather
# than deriving one from another); `#` starts a comment. The same file goes to osv-gate.py
# and to trivy as --ignorefile, so keep it in that format. Every entry names the issue that
# removes it and an expiry ("until YYYY-MM-DD"); delete it when that issue lands. Do not
# add osv-gate.py's `pkg:` scope field: trivy reads this file in its plain format, which
# ignores `pkg:`, so a scope would narrow only the osv-scanner gate.
#
# No accepted advisories: the image passes the gate with this file empty. Keep the file
# (with no ids) so both scanners always read the same, explicit list.
